==English==

===Etymology===
* First attested in 1611.
* {{sense|motor vehicle}} First attested in 1900.
* {{suffix|en|accelerate|or}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ək.ˈsɛl.ə.ˌɹeɪ.tɚ/|/æk.ˈsɛl.ə.ˌɹeɪ.tɚ/|/ɪk.ˈsɛl.ə.ˌɹeɪ.tɚ/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-accelerator.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who, or that which, [[accelerate]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The Second World War is said to have been a great '''accelerator''' for many scientific findings.}}
# A [[device]] for causing [[acceleration]].
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A substance which speeds up chemical reactions.
# {{lb|en|vehicle}} A [[pedal]] causing the vehicle to accelerate when it is pressed.
#: {{ux|en|As soon as you get onto the slipway, push the '''accelerator'''.}}
# {{lb|en|photography}} A [[chemical]] that reduces [[development]] time.
# {{lb|en|physics}} A device that accelerates charged [[subatomic]] [[particles]]; a [[particle accelerator]].
# {{lb|en|physiology|medical}} A [[muscle]] or [[nerve]] that speeds the performance of an action.
# {{lb|en|computing}} An [[accelerator key]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Davis Howard Chapman|title=Sams Teach Yourself Visual C++ .NET in 21 Days|page=187|passage=If they had allowed single-character '''accelerators''', Windows wouldn't be able to determine whether the character was input or a shortcut.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A computer component using dedicated hardware to accelerate the processing and display of graphics.
# {{lb|en|historical}} A light [[van]] to take [[mail]]s between a [[post office]] and a [[railway station]].
# {{lb|en|business}} A program for [[startup]] companies.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Tad Friend|date=2016-10-03 |title=Sam Altman’s Manifest Destiny |url=https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2016/10/10/sam-altmans-manifest-destiny||work=The New Yorker |passage=All the founders were graduates of Y Combinator, the startup “'''accelerator'''” that Graham co-founded: a three-month boot camp, run twice a year, in how to become a “unicorn”—Valleyspeak for a billion-dollar company.}}

